   "id": "sanhedrin.109b.11",
   "daf": "109b",
   "sentenceId": 10,
   "he": "עֲדַת קֹרַח אֵין לָהֶם חֵלֶק לָעוֹלָם הַבָּא שֶׁנֶּאֱמַר 'וַתְּכַס עֲלֵיהֶם הָאָרֶץ' בָּעוֹלָם הַזֶּה 'וַיֹּאבְדוּ מִתּוֹךְ הַקָּהָל' לָעוֹלָם הַבָּא דִּבְרֵי רַבִּי עֲקִיבָא רַבִּי אֱלִיעֶזֶר אוֹמֵר עֲלֵיהֶם אָמַר הַכָּתוּב 'ה' מֵמִית וּמְחַיֶּה מוֹרִיד שְׁאוֹל וַיָּעַל'",
   "en": "The members of «the assembly of Korah have no share in the World-to-Come, as it is stated: “And the earth closed upon them”» (Numbers 16:33), meaning «in this world,» and also: «“And they perished from among the assembly”» (Numbers 16:33), meaning «in the World-to-Come;» this is «the statement of Rabbi Akiva. Rabbi Eliezer says: About» the assembly of Korah, «the verse states: “The Lord kills and makes alive; He lowers to the grave, and raises”» (I Samuel 2:6), indicating that the assembly of Korah has a share in the World-to-Come."
  }
